### The One Hurdle: "Private" vs "Public" IP Addresses

* When you are inside your home, your router gives you an IP like **`192.168.1.1`**.
* But `192.168.1.1` is a **private address**—it only exists inside your house. If your friend at their house types `192.168.1.1`, their browser looks at *their own* router, not yours!
